(Q/'COHORT-REVIEW.md').write_text('# FX22 engineering assembly review\n\nOriginal atlas 06 row 2 contains brass nut, steel bolt, stones, gold impact and blue repair effects. The original1536x1024 RGBA board carries a cloudy backing; mode alone is not alpha proof. The replacement sources are genuine transparent1254-square images. No wrench or hammer has been invented.\n\n## Phase interpretation\n\n1. loose-hardware: tilted threaded bolt beside the open nut hole, two tiny spark strokes and two airborne chips.\n2. seating-impact: angled bolt tip enters the hole at a localized gold flash; four airborne chips accompany it.\n3. repair-swirl: upright fitted bolt, warm reflected head light and a blue ribbon passing behind/in front of the shaft.\n4. finished-fit: upright completed hardware, cool steel head, one blue star and three blue shards. Four grounded stones remain throughout.\n\n## Motion and registration caveats\n\n'+'\n'.join('- '+c for c in caveats)+'\n\n## Verification\n\nActual full-source black/white composites and colored overview were inspected. Native32/64 cells were inspected on black, white, bright stone, green ground, dark earth and checker. Full1–2–3–4 and terminal3–4–1–2 comparisons were inspected. The terminal comparison is not a runtime loop. Final parent static review is pending.\n\nSource perimeter maxima are0,0,0,1 with clean composites; all exports have two logical pixels of alpha0 border. All28 APNGs and112 decoded frames match expected exports. Four equal1/12-second frames and one play are encoded in14 canonical previews;14 slow repeating diagnostics are separate. Actual playback remains unobserved.\n')
(R/'README.md').write_text('# C01-FX-22 / 工程修复\n\nFour independently authored genuine RGBA phases from five built-in imagegen requests. One rejected repair-swirl omitted the four fixed stones; one bounded restoration supplied the selected replacement. Every request, prompt, raw/master source, reference snapshot and rejection is retained.\n\nIntegration: integration-catalog.json is the strict payload. Common1254-square canvas, scale28/1254, origin[2,2], source pivot[627,627], native32/64 and two logical transparent border pixels. No per-frame fit, alpha cleanup, code motion or fading.\n\nContract: four equal12fps frames, nonloop, one play,1/3second. No current authored FX22 consumer or scene lifecycle. The bolt articulates; the nut and four ground stones retain their identity with the documented0.558–0.625 logical-pixel full-sequence registration spread.\n\nReview: final-review.json and qa/COHORT-REVIEW.md contain the source/phase caveats. Motion proof, source-edge proof and APNG timing proof are linked there. Final parent static review is pending; actual playback is unobserved.\n\nComplete file hashes: deliverable-manifest.json excludes itself. No repository or Git writes were made by this task.\n')
